# Question: when a second signal arrives while the daemon's stop drain waits
# for a container that ignores its stop signal, is the container killed at
# once, rather than at the end of its stop timeout, with nothing of it left
# on the host (spec-container-1-runtime, the container-drain-second-signal-kills
# test, the lifecycle scenario "a signal arrives during the stop")?
#
# A unit test cannot decide it: TestForcedDrainKillsAtOnce proves the
# supervisor kills when the drain's context ends, and what this asks is
# whether the real daemon's abort of the drain reaches the plugin and ends
# the container before the daemon is gone.
#
# Method: the probe's drive mode starts the daemon itself, because a .ci line
# cannot send a signal between two observations. The container (a "stubborn"
# name, so it records its stop signal and keeps running) has a stop timeout of
# 30 seconds. Once it runs, drive sends SIGTERM, waits until the container
# recorded the stop signal, so the drain is under way, then sends a second
# SIGTERM and waits for the daemon to exit. The container must then be gone,
# less than 20 seconds after its stop signal.
#
# The store lives under /run, not in the test's work directory: in the QEMU
# guest that directory is on the 9p share of the checkout, and an overlay
# cannot take a 9p directory as its upper layer.
option=needs-linux:caps=sys-admin
option=exclusive:group=container
option=timeout:value=150s
option=env:var=ze.test.container.store:value=/run/ze-container-test-$PORT

tmpfs=container.conf:terminator=EOF_CONFIG
container {
	instance stubborn {
		stop-timeout 30;
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-containerprobe reset /run/ze-container-test-$PORT:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-containerprobe drive /run/ze-container-test-$PORT stubborn container.conf second-signal:timeout=120s:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the container runs
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the container received its stop signal while the daemon drains
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its control group is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its root mount is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: its runtime library state is gone
expect=stdout:contains=probe: it ended less than 20s after its stop signal
reject=stdout:contains=probe: FAIL
